ile's OpenStreetMap outlines, not photographs (none reachable): the outlines show the museum's point on a narrow terrace that runs north-north-east to south-south-west between two streets, about 35 degrees off the grid, so the whole street front (the gallery and its two neighbours, the pavement, its trees and the road) was turned 55 degrees to lie along that terrace with its glazed front toward the street on the east-south-east, and set 4 m east onto it (on 36% before, 72% now); the boxes became turned meshes and the glass was thickened to half a metre so it still shows; the site grown to 50 m square. Still guessed: which street the front faces, the neighbours' form, every height."}